{"date":"Thursday 26 November 2026","updated":"12:00","sub":"Thursday 26 November 2026 · GBP/USD. Watches the London killzone so you do not have to trade it: a map at 06:40, the leg and its equilibrium at 10:00, a scorecard at noon. It never calls a trade.","feed":"<article class=\"post\"><div class=\"time\">06:40<small>Morning map</small></div><div class=\"body\"><span class=\"tag\" style=\"--k:var(--blue)\">Morning map</span><h2>The nearest real draw is the Asia high, 18 pips above.</h2><p class=\"lede\">Before London opens, this is where the resting orders are and how often price has gone to get them by noon.</p><div class=\"plan\"><header><strong>GBP/USD · 1.31010</strong><span class=\"side map\">DRAW MAP</span></header><div class=\"pools\"><div class=\"pool\"><div class=\"nm\">Asia low<small>1.30965 · 4.5p below</small></div><div class=\"meter\"><i style=\"--p:57%\"></i></div><div class=\"odds\">57%</div></div><div class=\"pool\"><div class=\"nm\">Asia high<small>1.31195 · 18.5p above</small></div><div class=\"meter\"><i style=\"--p:40%\"></i></div><div class=\"odds\">40%</div></div><div class=\"pool\"><div class=\"nm\">Last week's low<small>1.30757 · 25.3p below</small></div><div class=\"meter\"><i style=\"--p:18%\"></i></div><div class=\"odds\">18%</div></div><div class=\"pool\"><div class=\"nm\">Yesterday's high<small>1.31305 · 29.5p above</small></div><div class=\"meter\"><i style=\"--p:15%\"></i></div><div class=\"odds\">15%</div></div><div class=\"pool\"><div class=\"nm\">Yesterday's low<small>1.30459 · 55.1p below</small></div><div class=\"meter\"><i style=\"--p:2%\"></i></div><div class=\"odds\">2%</div></div></div></div><p>Nearest draw of 10 pips or more: GBP/USD Asia high 1.31195 (18.5 pips above, 40% reached historically); EUR/USD previous week low 1.09537 (10.1 pips below). Times unverified today: the feed-clock check disagreed between pairs and was pinned to the documented offset, and the economic calendar could not be fetched (US Thanksgiving).</p><p class=\"dim\">Watching only. Handover at 10:00.</p><section class=\"stage\" aria-label=\"Session chart\"><header><div><strong id=\"cPair\"></strong><small>15m · UK time</small></div><div class=\"views\" id=\"views\"></div></header>\n<svg class=\"chart\" id=\"chart\" viewBox=\"0 0 760 420\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Candlestick chart of the session with the desk's levels\"></svg><div class=\"pdk\" id=\"pdk\"></div><div class=\"scap\" id=\"cap\"></div></section></div></article>\n<article class=\"post\"><div class=\"time\">10:00<small>Handover</small></div><div class=\"body\"><span class=\"tag\" style=\"--k:var(--copper)\">Killzone handover</span><h2>A 22-pip leg up. Equilibrium is 1.31094.</h2><div class=\"plan\"><header><strong>GBP/USD</strong><span class=\"side map\">HANDOVER</span></header><dl><dt>Leg</dt><dd><span class=\"px \">1.30983</span> at 07:55 → <span class=\"px \">1.31204</span> at 09:25 · 22.1 pips up</dd><dt>Equilibrium</dt><dd><span class=\"px c\">1.31094</span> · 2.7 pips above price · returns by noon on <b>65%</b> of sessions</dd><dt>Swept</dt><dd>Asia high <span class=\"px \">1.31195</span>, 1 pips past</dd></dl></div><p>The killzone lifted both pairs through their Asia highs, and both slipped back to sit a few pips under the equilibrium of the morning leg. Both pairs took the same side, so there is no SMT. The Asia lows and yesterday's highs are still untouched.</p></div></article>\n<article class=\"post\"><div class=\"time\">12:00<small>Scorecard</small></div><div class=\"body\"><span class=\"tag\" style=\"--k:var(--gold)\">Scorecard</span><h2>Equilibrium came back by noon.</h2><div class=\"plan\"><header><strong>GBP/USD</strong><span class=\"side res\">SCORECARD</span></header><dl><dt>Equilibrium 1.31094</dt><dd><span class=\"g\">Reached</span> at 10:00</dd><dt>Asia low 1.30965</dt><dd><span class=\"g\">Reached</span> at 11:15</dd><dt>Asia high 1.31195</dt><dd><span class=\"g\">Reached</span> at 09:15</dd><dt>Last week's low 1.30757</dt><dd><span class=\"r\">Not reached</span></dd><dt>Trades called</dt><dd>None. This desk names levels; it does not call a side.</dd></dl></div><p>A fake-out morning: London ran the Asia high on both pairs, came back to equilibrium straight after 10:00, then GBP/USD fell through to take its Asia low by 11:25.</p></div></article>","week":"<section class=\"week\"><h3>Meridian 2 · week of 23 Nov · equilibrium reached by noon</h3><div class=\"wk\"><div class=\"\"><small>Mon</small><b class=\"\">—</b></div><div class=\"\"><small>Tue</small><b class=\"r\">no</b></div><div class=\"\"><small>Wed</small><b class=\"g\">yes</b></div><div class=\"\"><small>Thu</small><b class=\"g\">yes</b></div><div class=\"\"><small>Fri</small><b class=\"\">—</b></div><div class=\"tot\"><small>Week</small><b class=\"\">—</b></div></div></section>","chart":{"pair":"GBP/USD","bars":[["00:00",1.31111,1.31157,1.31097,1.31137],["00:15",1.31141,1.31143,1.31106,1.31118],["00:30",1.31114,1.31141,1.31113,1.31139],["00:45",1.31138,1.31195,1.31124,1.31194],["01:00",1.3119,1.31192,1.31154,1.31155],["01:15",1.31157,1.3119,1.31129,1.3113],["01:30",1.31132,1.3114,1.31088,1.31089],["01:45",1.3109,1.3111,1.31067,1.31088],["02:00",1.31082,1.31127,1.31082,1.31124],["02:15",1.31121,1.31179,1.31121,1.31155],["02:30",1.31151,1.31167,1.31137,1.31147],["02:45",1.31149,1.31156,1.31077,1.31081],["03:00",1.31077,1.31084,1.31038,1.31043],["03:15",1.31041,1.31052,1.31016,1.31034],["03:30",1.31031,1.31039,1.30965,1.30983],["03:45",1.30979,1.31005,1.30977,1.31004],["04:00",1.30998,1.31012,1.30971,1.31007],["04:15",1.30995,1.31036,1.30995,1.31025],["04:30",1.31026,1.31063,1.31019,1.31055],["04:45",1.31044,1.31074,1.31005,1.31025],["05:00",1.31023,1.31047,1.30999,1.31023],["05:15",1.31018,1.31067,1.31014,1.3103],["05:30",1.31026,1.31033,1.30984,1.30997],["05:45",1.30991,1.31023,1.30979,1.31019],["06:00",1.31012,1.31051,1.30998,1.31042],["06:15",1.31031,1.31053,1.3102,1.31029],["06:30",1.31027,1.31027,1.30989,1.30991],["06:45",1.30998